{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He shall not defile himself, a husband, among his people, to profane himself.</b> He shall not defile himself to a disqualified wife with whom he is profaned while she is still with him. And so the plain sense of the verse: a husband shall not defile himself to his kin while he is among his people — who have people to bury them, so that she is not a met mitzvah. And which kin have I spoken of? To that which is לְהֵחַלּוֹ — that he become profaned from his priesthood (see Sifra; Yevamot 90a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:30.816446671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}